For a replaced grid item’s min-content contribution in the inline
axis, Ladybird now resolves a percentage max-width against zero.
Blink, WebKit and Gecko all do the same, also only in the inline
axis. Blink’s ComputeMinAndMaxContentContributionForReplaced() takes
just the min size as the min-content contribution when LogicalWidth()
or LogicalMaxWidth() has a percentage. WebKit’s RenderReplaced::
computeIntrinsicLogicalWidthContributions() sets the min-content
contribution to zero in that case. And Gecko’s AddIntrinsicSizeOffset()
in nsLayoutUtils.cpp applies the compressible min-content rule only in
the inline axis, for web compatibility.
